# No local deploy; git depends on agent environment

**Deploy** is owned by CI: Cloudflare Workers Builds / Modal on prod and stable
dev, plus GitHub Actions `preview-stack.yml` for **dev-account ephemeral
backend stacks only** (ADR 0027). **Git** depends on where the agent runs.

## All agents — do not deploy from the agent environment

- Do not run `wrangler deploy`, `pnpm deploy`, `deploy:dev`, `deploy:prod`, `versions:upload`, `preview:upload`, `modal deploy`, or any other local deploy/publish
- Do not work around deploy via `pnpm dlx wrangler@latest deploy` or Cloudflare write APIs that publish a Worker
- Do not run `preview-stack.mjs up` from a laptop — that is the GitHub Action on the dev account
- Tell the user when a change needs a deploy; they ship via the existing pipeline

## Local / desktop agents — do not commit or push

When running in Cursor Desktop (or any local workspace session):

- Do **not** `git commit`, `git push`, `git tag`, or create commits via other tools unless the user **explicitly** asks in that message
- Do not amend, rebase onto remote, or force-push
- Leave staging, committing, and pushing to the user

## Cloud agents — commit, push, and open a PR into `dev`

When running as a **cloud agent** (Background Agent, Cloud Agent, Bugbot fix agent, or similar remote VM checkout):

- Start from **`origin/dev`** unless the user named another base (`main` / hotfix / `/promote`). `harness` has no `dev` — stay on `main`.
- **Do** create conventional commits and push the working branch so the work is reviewable and CI can run
- **Do** open a PR **into `dev`** (not `main`). Worker `preview.yml` and library `preview-publish.yml` only run on PRs targeting `dev`. That is the polyrepo preview system (ADR 0027) — use it; do not add label `no-preview` unless asked
- Prefer small, focused commits; follow that repo's commitlint / conventional-commit config
- Still **never** local-deploy — do not run `preview:upload` or `preview-stack.mjs` from the agent. Workers Builds / `preview-stack.yml` ship the preview
- After the PR is open, report the preview URLs. Slug: `node scripts/preview-slug.mjs <branch>` (or the harness copy). Frontends: `https://<slug>-<worker>.livo-tv.workers.dev`. Services: `https://<svc>-<slug>.livo-tv.workers.dev`. Optional e2e: `cd e2e && pnpm test:preview --slug <slug>`
- iOS TestFlight public link: label the `ios-app` PR `ios-preview`
- Avoid force-push to `main`/`master`/`dev`; do not skip hooks unless the user explicitly requires it
